 *     <li>If the string is {@code null}, it returns {@code null}.</li>
 *     <li>If the string is blank (empty or whitespace only), it throws {@code NumberFormatException}.</li>
 *     <li>**Hexadecimal Numbers:** If the string starts with a hexadecimal prefix (e.g., "0x", "-0X", "#"),
 *         it attempts to parse it as an {@code Integer}, then {@code Long}, and finally {@code BigInteger}
 *         using base-16 interpretation.</li>
 *     <li>**Suffix-Hinted Numbers:** If the string ends with a type-hinting character:
 *         <ul>
 *             <li>'l' or 'L': Attempts to parse as a {@code Long}. If it overflows, it falls back to {@code BigInteger}.
 *                 A decimal point or exponent with an 'l'/'L' suffix will result in a {@code NumberFormatException}.</li>
